; Colour-code screen key graphics
;
; Four 16x16 pixel graphics, 32 bytes each (16 rows of 2 bytes): the keys
; 1, 2, 3 and 4 shown in rows 10-11 of the code screen. Drawn by #R$86C3 with
; #R$9456 at columns 2, 5, 8 and 11. Their colours come from the attributes
; at #R$9B80: most pixels are set (key colour as ink) and the digit is made of
; unset pixels, which show black on the black paper.
